    <!-- ── First-run explainer ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <string name="intro_title">Why we ask about your health</string>
    <string name="intro_body_1">The same air does not affect everyone equally — asthma, heart conditions, pregnancy, older age and young children all change the picture.</string>
    <string name="intro_body_2">Once you fill in your age group and any conditions, the AI advisor tailors its advice to you, and the suggestions on the home screen follow suit.</string>
    <string name="intro_body_3">By default this stays on your device only, and you can change or clear it at any time.</string>
    <string name="intro_fill_now">Fill it in</string>
    <string name="intro_later">Maybe later</string>

    <!-- ── User guide ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <string name="user_guide_text">This app gives you live air quality data for Taiwan along with personal health guidance. Here is what each screen does:\n\n1. Home\n- The live AQI and air quality level from the station nearest to you.\n- Tap the icon at the top right to switch between GPS location and your saved places.\n\n2. AI advisor\n- Personal health advice based on your health profile and the air right now.\n\n3. Report (the orange button in the middle)\n- Spotted a fire, an odour or dust? File a report with the place and a description.\n\n4. Alerts\n- Forecasts, warnings and reports filed by people near you.\n- Tap the map icon at the top right for official fire alerts and a hotspot map.\n\n5. Settings\n- Turn the daily air quality notification on or off and choose when it arrives.\n- Edit your health profile (kept on this device by default) and decide whether the server may use it to warn you first.\n- Add saved places so you can switch between them quickly.\n- Switch the app language (繁體中文 / English).</string>

